'''bogue<sup>3</sup>''' (bōg), ''n.'' [OF., = F. ''bouche'': see ''embogue''.] A mouth; an embouchure. {{smaller|Used specifically in the name ''the Bogue'', the principal mouth of the Canton river in China (also called ''Boca Tigris'', the Tiger’s Mouth).}}

'''boguest''' (bō′gest), ''n.'' [E. dial., appar. ''barguest'' varied toward ''bogy''<sup>1</sup>: see these words.] A specter; a ghost. [Prov. Eng. (Yorkshire).]

